## 🔍 Assignment 4: Design and Develop Custom Application (Mini Project) using Salesforce Cloud

---

### 🎯 Objective

Create a custom application in Salesforce using **point-and-click tools** — no code. This involves:
- Creating a custom object (like a table)
- Creating tabs and apps to manage it
- Testing it in both web and mobile views

---

## ✅ Step-by-Step Detailed Guide

---

### 🔹 Step 1: Open Salesforce (Lightning Experience)

Make sure you are in **Lightning Experience** (modern UI of Salesforce):
1. Log in to [https://login.salesforce.com](https://login.salesforce.com)
2. Switch to **Lightning** (if not already there) by clicking on your avatar > "Switch to Lightning Experience"

---

### 🔹 Step 2: Create a Custom Object

You’re building a "Comment Box" app, so first create a **custom object**:

1. Click on the **gear icon (⚙️)** → then click **Setup**.
2. In the **Quick Find box**, type **Objects** and click **Object Manager**.
3. Click **Create → Custom Object**.
4. Fill out the form as below:

| Field            | Value             |
|------------------|------------------|
| Label            | `Comment`        |
| Plural Label     | `Comments`       |
| Object Name      | auto-filled as `Comment__c` |
| Record Name      | `Comment Name` (or anything suitable) |
| Data Type        | `Text` (or Text Area if it's a full comment) |
| Allow Reports    | ✅ Check this |
| Launch New Tab   | ✅ Check this (optional) |
| Deployment Status| Deployed         |

5. Click **Save**.

✅ You now have a custom object in Salesforce that represents comments.

---

### 🔹 Step 3: Create a Custom Tab for Your Object

1. In **Setup**, search for **Tabs** in the Quick Find box.
2. Click on **Tabs**.
3. Under **Custom Object Tabs**, click **New**.
4. Set up the tab:

| Field        | Value                |
|--------------|----------------------|
| Object       | `Comment`            |
| Tab Style    | Choose any icon you like |
| Description  | (Optional) Add one   |

5. Click **Next → Next → Save**.

✅ Now you can view and interact with "Comments" from the UI like any built-in object (e.g., Accounts).

---

### 🔹 Step 4: Create a Custom App for the Mini Project

1. In **Setup**, search for **App Manager**.
2. Click **App Manager**.
3. Click **New Lightning App** (top right).
4. Fill out the form:

#### Section 1: App Details
| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| App Name | `Comment Box` |
| App Label | `Comment Box` |
| Description | (Optional) |

Click **Next**.

#### Section 2: App Options

- Leave the default options selected
- Click **Next**

#### Section 3: Navigation Items

- Search for and select:  
  ✅ `Contacts`  
  ✅ `Comment` (the custom object)

Click **Next**.

#### Section 4: Assign User Profiles

- Select: ✅ **System Administrator**
- Move it to the "Selected Profiles" side
- Click **Save and Finish**

✅ Now you've created a full app to manage comments.

---

### 🔹 Step 5: Use the App (Web & Mobile)

#### 🖥 Web View

1. Go to the **App Launcher (9-dot grid icon)**.
2. Search for and click **Comment Box**.
3. You'll see the app you just built with tabs for **Contacts** and **Comments**.

#### 📱 Simulate Mobile View

Salesforce has a mobile app, but you can **simulate it in Chrome**:

1. Open your **Comment Box app** in Chrome.
2. Right-click anywhere on the screen and click **Inspect**.
3. In Developer Tools, click the **Toggle Device Toolbar (mobile icon)**.
4. Reload the page if needed.

✅ Now you can test how your app would look in the **Salesforce Mobile App**.

---

### 🔹 Step 6: Add a Comment Record

1. In the app, go to the **Comments tab**.
2. Click **New**.
3. Fill in the comment data and click **Save**.

🎉 You've now created your first comment record using your custom app!

---

## ✅ Conclusion

You have:
- Designed a custom object (`Comment`)
- Created a tab and added it to a new Lightning App
- Simulated a mobile version
- Created and saved data records

This is how Salesforce allows **non-developers** to build apps quickly using clicks, not code.

---

